# Fork vs upstream (`jumpserver/clients`)

This repo tracks official `dev` but is **not** a thin overlay. Keep our branch (`dev`). Do not `reset --hard` to upstream.

**Keep (do not take upstream replacements):**
- Rust `local_app_launcher` (no `go-client`)
- UI HTTP asset/detail APIs (no `asset_actions` / `useAssetFetcher` event bus)
- `{asset_name}` template, `jms://`, Warp / Warp CN, `.jscplugin` CI

**Version:** source `package.json` / `Cargo.toml` / `tauri.conf.json` / `ui/app.config.ts` match the latest official **release tag** (e.g. `v4.1.7` → `4.1.7`). CI still overwrites the string on tag via `pnpm run set_version`.

**Periodic upstream sync:** `git fetch upstream && git merge upstream/dev`. On conflicts, keep our launcher/UI; then **port the bugfix into our files** (same behavior, current architecture). Skip if already present. After merge, bump the version string if official tagged a newer release.

Ahead-of-upstream commit count is expected. Behind must stay 0.
